  "_comment": [
    "Rows lifted verbatim from Jason's Vista Payroll Workbook detail review",
    "(week ending 9-05-26). Read out of the PDF character by character and",
    "assigned to columns by the report's own ruling lines, so these are the",
    "report's values rather than a guess at them.",
    "",
    "Only rows where no cell overflows its column are used. Long text such as",
    "'Transmission / Power Train' or 'Shop Administration' spills visually into",
    "the next column, so reading it back gives a fragment - and a test that",
    "asserted on a fragment would be asserting on something the report does",
    "not hold. Those rows are left out rather than half-checked. The columns",
    "are still covered by the shorter values, and the export does not",
    "transform that text in any case.",
    "",
    "Holiday lines are left out too: nobody clocks in for a holiday, so the",
    "shop never books one and the export has no opinion about them."
  ],
